# Backend configuration for local development.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and adjust, or export the
# variables in your shell. On a host such as Render, set them in the service's
# Environment tab and mark the secrets as secret.
#
# Nothing in here is required to run locally: every value has a development
# default. `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is the exception in production (see below).

# ── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Password for the bootstrap `admin` account — the only account that can list or
# delete users and download the raw databases. The development default is
# `demo123`; a production deployment (NODE_ENV=production) refuses to start
# without an explicit value, because that default is public knowledge.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ── Server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Render sets PORT for you.
# PORT=8080

# ── Database files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults resolve against the backend's working directory (`backend/db/`).
# On Render, attach a persistent disk and point these at its mount path —
# without that, every deploy starts from empty databases.
# TX_DB_PATH=./db/tx.db
# SPOT_FUTURE_DB_PATH=./db/spotFuture.db
# FUNDING_RATE_DB_PATH=./db/fRate.db
# On Render:
# TX_DB_PATH=/data/tx.db
# SPOT_FUTURE_DB_PATH=/data/spotFuture.db
# FUNDING_RATE_DB_PATH=/data/fRate.db

# ── Demo data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Days of history seeded for an account that asks for demo data (default 1095).
# DEMO_WINDOW_DAYS=1095
